* BP321: single-supply CMOS op-amp, SOT-23-5. Behavioural macro-model: 100 dB DC gain, 1 MHz gain-bandwidth,
* a second pole at 3 MHz, 100 ohm open-loop output resistance, 8 nV/rtHz white input voltage noise at 27 C.
* No output swing limit, no slew limit, no input bias current.
* Written for Backplane's simulation benchmark (test/ksim_bench). It is not a manufacturer's model of any part.
*
* Connections:  non-inverting input
*               |   inverting input
*               |   |   positive supply
*               |   |   |   negative supply
*               |   |   |   |   output
*               |   |   |   |   |
.subckt BP321   inp inn vcc vee out
Rnoise nz 0 3861.33
Enoise inx inp nz 0 1
Rm1 vcc mid 1meg noisy=0
Rm2 mid vee 1meg noisy=0
Rinp inx mid 1e12 noisy=0
Rinn inn mid 1e12 noisy=0
G1 0 n1 inx inn 1m
R1 n1 0 100meg noisy=0
C1 n1 0 159.155p
E2 n2 0 n1 0 1
R2 n2 n3 1k noisy=0
C2 n3 0 53.0516p
Eout n4 n5 n3 0 1
Emid n5 0 mid 0 1
Rout n4 out 100 noisy=0
.ends BP321
